{"candidates":[{"content":"Add an incremental maintenance layer for the grounded fixed point: when attack edges are added or removed, recompute only the affected region of the label computation rather than the whole graph, exploiting that labels are a pure function of the graph (0e806619395ec8f4). Determinism is preserved because the incremental result must equal a full recomputation, enforced by a deterministic spot-check over a hash-selected edge subset; polynomial cost becomes amortized-polynomial over a batch of edits. The criticizable claim: incremental correctness requires a stable node ordering and tie-breaking rule that the current fixpoint (09ffabcd92979168) does not specify, so the proposal silently adds an order-dependence that must be made explicit and verified.","typicality":0.3,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4"},{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Strengthen skepticism across conditioning regimes by computing the grounded extension on a family of school-projected attack subgraphs — each projection a deterministic function of the graph per registered school (1958b39701612057) — and committing only the intersection of all grounded extensions; refutation then commits only for nodes outside the union. Determinism and polynomial cost hold if the school set is fixed and each projection is linear in edge count. The criticizable point: the intersection of several grounded extensions is not itself a Dung grounded extension, so reinstatement must be re-derived and may fail on nodes that are reinstated in every projection yet suspended in the intersection, weakening the very guarantee being extended.","typicality":0.2,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"1958b39701612057"},{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Derive a refutation-depth label alongside accept/refute/suspend without changing the skeptical semantics: a node is refuted at depth k when it is attacked by a node accepted at depth k-1, depths resolved by node-id tie-break so the computation remains a pure deterministic function of the graph and stays polynomial. The criticizable claim: depth is not invariant under isomorphic relabelling because the tie-break depends on node ids, and on cyclic attack chains the depth labels may be unstable or misleading, so the derived grading could be presented as meaningful evidence when it is an artifact of ordering.","typicality":0.45,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"},{"block":"0e806619395ec8f4"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Emit, in the same pass as the fixed point, a minimal witness subgraph for every committed label: for a refuted node, the accepted attacker chain; for an accepted node, the absence of any accepted attacker within the extension; for a suspended node, the vacuous empty witness. Witness choice uses a deterministic tie-break so the whole computation stays a pure function of the graph and each witness is bounded by edge count, preserving polynomial cost. The criticizable point: minimal-witness selection may require a global minimization that breaks locality and cannot be computed incrementally, and vacuous witnesses for suspended nodes invite a false reading that suspension is evidenced when it is precisely the absence of a decision.","typicality":0.35,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"},{"block":"1dd041117ca8c54a"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Maintain carriage-closure as an explicit invariant that expands the edge set the grounded semantics sees without touching the fixpoint algorithm: whenever an artifact carries a warrant naming a target, every attacker of the carrier becomes an attacker of the warrant, enforced at att-construction time (0974daebd1665965, 0378275f89478d38). Because closure is a deterministic, linear-time expansion of the attack relation, the existing fixed point is unchanged and determinism, polynomial cost, reinstatement-as-derived, and root validity all survive verbatim. The criticizable claim: closure can manufacture self-attack cycles that newly refute previously accepted carriers, and the rule must be shown to be confluent — independent of the order in which edges are added — or it introduces an order-dependence into the committed edge set.","typicality":0.55,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"0974daebd1665965"},{"block":"0378275f89478d38"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]},{"content":"Separate 'not-yet-decided' from 'genuinely undecidable' by computing a second derived fixed point — the co-grounded (greatest) extension — on the same graph and tagging suspended nodes: nodes in the grounded extension's undecided region but outside the co-grounded region are flagged 'structurally refutable pending evidence', while nodes in the intersection are flagged 'genuinely undecidable'. Both fixed points are deterministic and polynomial, and reinstatement remains a derived property of each. The criticizable point: the co-grounded extension is credulous, so using it as a suspension flag leaks credulous commitments into the skeptical guarantee unless the flag is strictly advisory, and the proposal must prove the two fixed points cannot disagree on the committed accept/refute sets in a way that undermines root validity.","typicality":0.25,"evidence_refs":[{"block":"09ffabcd92979168"},{"block":"0c302d11d621778b"}],"neighbours":["SRC_001"]}]}